1
00:06:31,578 --> 00:06:37,578
Walking with the Enemy is a action, drama,
history film directed by Mark Schmidt.

2
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:09,157
Regent Horthy is the leader of Hungary and a German ally, but his favorable
standing with Hitler changes as the war comes to an end.

3
00:19:34,736 --> 00:19:40,736
Forced to cede Hungary’s power or else witness the execution of his son, Regent Horthy gives up control of his
country to the Nazis, who quickly move Hungarians to ghettos and death camps, with no hope in sight.

4
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:12,315
But the despair changes when a young man named Elek emerges.

5
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:43,894
Separated from his family during the relocations and aided by the woman
he loves , Elek defies the enemy by becoming one of them.

6
00:39:09,473 --> 00:39:15,473
In a race against time, disguised as a Nazi Officer he embarks on a
mission to save his family and thousands of his countrymen.

7
00:45:41,052 --> 00:45:47,052
Elek Cohen, played by Jonas Armstrong.

8
00:52:12,631 --> 00:52:18,631
Hannah Schoen, played by Hannah Tointon.

9
00:58:44,210 --> 00:58:50,210
Regent Miklos Horthy, played by Ben Kingsley.

10
01:05:15,789 --> 01:05:21,789
Miklos Schoen, played by Simon Dutton.

11
01:11:47,368 --> 01:11:53,368
Lt. Colonel Otto Skorzeny, played by Burn Gorman.

12
01:18:18,947 --> 01:18:24,947
Miklos Horthy Jr., played by Shane Taylor.

13
01:24:50,526 --> 01:24:56,526
Walking with the Enemy is a 2014 American action drama film directed by
Mark Schmidt, and scripted by Kenny Golde and Mark Schmidt.

14
01:31:22,105 --> 01:31:28,105
The film stars Jonas Armstrong, Ben Kingsley, Simon Kunz, Hannah
Tointon, Simon Dutton, Burn Gorman, and Charles Hubbell.

15
01:37:53,684 --> 01:37:59,684
It is inspired by the true story of Pinchas Tibor Rosenbaum.

16
01:44:25,263 --> 01:44:31,263
Set in Budapest and nearby villages, it depicts the German occupation of
Hungary during the final months of the Second World War.

17
01:50:56,842 --> 01:51:02,842
The story is about a young Hungarian-Jewish man, Elek Cohen (played by Jonas Armstrong), who dons an SS uniform to
pose as an officer to find out the fate of his family and to rescue fellow Jews from the Holocaust.

18
01:57:28,421 --> 01:57:34,421
The tone is emotional.
